"}},"outputId":"1f430786-dd00-42f1-d4de-9b035fd1987e"},"execution_count":397,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Potentially Problematic Records\n","==============================\n","\n","Zero-distance trips: 90201\n","Trips above 99th percentile distance: 34624\n","Trips above 99th percentile duration: 34725\n","Trips above 99th percentile speed: 34732\n","Zero-passenger trips: 24465\n","\n","These records should be investigated rather than automatically treated as invalid.\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Q112 - Important Data-Quality Limitations\n","\n","- Some records contain missing values, so not every trip has complete information.\n","- Some records contain unusual values such as zero distance, zero passenger count, very long duration, or very high speed.\n","- Location IDs represent TLC Taxi Zone IDs, so they do not directly provide neighborhood names without a separate lookup table.\n","- Extreme values were investigated but were not automatically removed because some may represent legitimate trips.\n","- The dataset covers January 2025 only, so the results may not represent other months or seasons.\n","- Correlation results show associations between variables and should not be interpreted as causal relationships.\n","- The dataset does not contain fare, tip, revenue, profit, customer ID, or driver ID information, so financial or customer-level conclusions cannot be made."],"metadata":{"id":"Dm8OWMQrtcwn"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Q113 - Operational Questions for Further Investigation\n","\n","Based on this analysis, a taxi company or transportation analyst could investigate:\n","\n","1. Which pickup locations experience the highest demand during peak hours?\n","\n","2. Which routes have consistently high demand across different days and time periods?\n","\n","3. How does trip duration vary between peak and off-peak periods?\n","\n","4. Which locations have unusually long trip durations?\n","\n","5. Are there specific routes where trip distance and duration differ substantially from the general pattern?\n","\n","6. Do vendor-level differences remain consistent across different hours and days?\n","\n","7. Which payment types are associated with different trip characteristics?\n","\n","8. Are unusual speed, distance, or duration records concentrated in particular locations or time periods?\n","\n","9. How does taxi demand change across different months and seasons?\n","\n","10. Would combining taxi-trip data with weather, traffic, or event data provide better explanations of demand and trip duration?"],"metadata":{"id":"k3rHT9SgvGoe"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Final KPI Summary\n","\n","kpi_summary = pd.Series({\n","    \"Total Trips\":\n","        len(clean_df),\n","\n","    \"Average Trip Distance\":\n","        clean_df[\"trip_distance\"].mean(),\n","\n","    \"Median Trip Distance\":\n","        clean_df[\"trip_distance\"].median(),\n","\n","    \"Average Trip Duration\":\n","        clean_df[\"trip_duration_minutes\"].mean(),\n","\n","    \"Median Trip Duration\":\n","        clean_df[\"trip_duration_minutes\"].median(),\n","\n","    \"Maximum Trip Distance\":\n","        clean_df[\"trip_distance\"].max(),\n","\n","    \"Maximum Trip Duration\":\n","        clean_df[\"trip_duration_minutes\"].max(),\n","\n","    \"Average Speed\":\n","        clean_df[\"average_speed_mph\"].mean(),\n","\n","    \"Most Common Passenger Count\":\n","        clean_df[\"passenger_count\"].mode()[0],\n","\n","    \"Busiest Pickup Hour\":\n","        clean_df[\"pickup_hour\"].value_counts().idxmax(),\n","\n","    \"Busiest Day\":\n","        clean_df[\"day_of_week\"].value_counts().idxmax(),\n","\n","    \"Most Common Payment Type\":\n","        clean_df[\"payment_type\"].mode()[0],\n","\n","    \"Most Common Pickup Location\":\n","        clean_df[\"PULocationID\"].mode()[0],\n","\n","    \"Most Common Drop-off Location\":\n","        clean_df[\"DOLocationID\"].mode()[0],\n","\n","    \"Most Common Route\":\n","        clean_df[\"route\"].mode()[0]\n","})\n","\n","print(\"Final KPI Summary:\")\n","print(kpi_summary)"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"hWTCh_UMtOHO","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1791315934561,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":834,"user":{"displayName":"Abu Sufiyan Siddi","userId":"17306214027502541703"}},"outputId":"8610cc75-2748-4eb6-9504-b773216a1862"},"execution_count":398,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Final KPI Summary:\n","Total Trips                          3473175\n","Average Trip Distance                5.85764\n","Median Trip Distance                    1.67\n","Average Trip Duration              15.041875\n","Median Trip Duration                    11.7\n","Maximum Trip Distance              276423.57\n","Maximum Trip Duration            5626.316667\n","Average Speed                      25.735527\n","Most Common Passenger Count              1.0\n","Busiest Pickup Hour                       18\n","Busiest Day                         Thursday\n","Most Common Payment Type                   1\n","Most Common Pickup Location              161\n","Most Common Drop-off Location            236\n","Most Common Route                 237 -> 236\n","dtype: object\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":[" # Key Findings\n","\n","### 1. Demand Pattern\n","Taxi demand varies considerably by pickup hour, with a clear difference between the busiest and least busy periods.\n","\n","### 2. Weekday vs Weekend\n","The distribution of trips differs between weekdays and weekends, showing that demand is not uniform throughout the week.\n","\n","### 3. Typical Trip\n","The median trip distance and median trip duration provide a useful description of a typical taxi trip and are less affected by extreme observations than the mean.\n","\n","### 4. Location Concentration\n","A relatively small number of pickup and drop-off Taxi Zone IDs account for a large share of observed trips.\n","\n","### 5. Route Concentration\n","Some routes occur much more frequently than others, indicating concentration of observed trip activity among particular location pairs.\n","\n","### 6. Distance and Duration\n","Trip distance and trip duration show a positive relationship, indicating that longer trips generally tend to be associated with longer durations.\n","\n","### 7. Passenger Patterns\n","One passenger is the most common passenger-count category, while other passenger counts occur less frequently.\n","\n","### 8. Payment Patterns\n","Some payment types are considerably more common than others, indicating that payment activity is not evenly distributed across categories.\n","\n","### 9. Vendor Differences\n","Average trip distance, duration, passenger count, and speed vary across vendors in the observed dataset.\n","\n","### 10. Unusual Records\n","The dataset contains potentially unusual observations involving distance, duration, passenger count, and calculated speed. These records were investigated rather than automatically removed.\n","\n","### 11. Data Quality\n","Several data-quality limitations should be considered when interpreting the results, including missing values, unusual observations, the January 2025 time period, and the use of Taxi Zone IDs instead of neighborhood names.\n","\n","### 12. Overall Observation\n","The analysis shows that taxi-trip activity varies by time, location, route, passenger count, payment type, vendor, and trip characteristics."],"metadata":{"id":"AkGtFiDKwP8t"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Limitations\n","\n","1. The dataset covers January 2025 only, so the results may not represent other months, seasons, or years.\n","\n","2. The dataset contains missing values in some fields, which can affect certain analyses.\n","\n","3. Some records contain unusual values such as zero distance, zero passenger count, very long trips, very long durations, or unusually high calculated speeds.\n","\n","4. Potential outliers were investigated but were not automatically removed because extreme observations may represent legitimate trips.\n","\n","5. PULocationID and DOLocationID are Taxi Zone IDs. They do not directly provide neighborhood names without an appropriate Taxi Zone lookup table.\n","\n","6. The dataset does not contain fare, tip, revenue, profit, customer ID, or driver ID information. Therefore, financial, profitability, and customer-level conclusions cannot be made.\n","\n","7. Average speed is calculated from trip distance and trip duration. Unusual timestamp or distance records can therefore produce unusual calculated speeds.\n","\n","8. Correlation analysis identifies associations between variables but does not establish causation.\n","\n","9. The analysis is based on the available recorded trip data and therefore may not capture external factors such as traffic, weather, road conditions, or special events.\n","\n","10. Vendor, payment, rate-code, and location identifiers describe categories in the dataset and should be interpreted according to the available data definitions."],"metadata":{"id":"ReyjfVQ8wo6Y"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Final Conclusion\n","\n","This project analyzed the NYC Yellow Taxi trip data for January 2025 using NumPy, Pandas, Matplotlib, and Seaborn.\n","\n","The analysis examined data quality, trip characteristics, time-based demand, passenger patterns, pickup and drop-off locations, routes, payment types, vendors, rate codes, store-and-forward trips, correlations, and potential anomalies.\n","\n","The results show that taxi activity varies across different hours, days, locations, routes, and trip characteristics. The analysis also identified differences in trip distance, duration, passenger count, payment type, vendor, and other categories.\n","\n","Trip distance and trip duration show an observable relationship, while the investigation of unusual records identified several observations that require caution when interpreting the results.\n","\n","Data cleaning and feature engineering were used to prepare the dataset for analysis while avoiding unnecessary removal of potentially legitimate observations. Potential outliers were investigated rather than automatically deleted.\n","\n","Overall, this project demonstrates how structured data analysis can be used to understand taxi-trip patterns and identify areas for further operational investigation.\n","\n","However, the conclusions are limited to the available January 2025 data and the variables contained in the dataset. The analysis does not support conclusions about revenue, profit, customers, drivers, or causal relationships.\n","\n","Further analysis using multiple months of taxi data together with traffic, weather, road-condition, and event information could provide a broader understanding of taxi demand and trip behavior."],"metadata":{"id":"-ggZqIV0wuMB"}}],"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyP+kbeGQAepu/Kxa3WETPXW"},"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0}